                and the special case of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+fibered+in+groupoids"} fibration fibered in groupoids
          %p
            The analog of this for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            are
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration"}> Cartesian fibration
                s
            %li
              %p
                the special case of left/right (Kan-)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations+of+quasi-categories"} fibrations of quasi-categories
          %p respectively.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to S
            is a
            %strong left fibration
            or
            %strong left Kan fibration
            if it has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            with respect to all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            inclusions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda[n]_k \to \Delta[n]
            except possibly the right outer ones:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \lt n
          %p
            It is a
            %strong right fibration
            or
            %strong right Kan fibration
            if its extends against all horns except possibly the left outer ones:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt k \leq n
          %p
            So
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to S
            is a left fibration precisely if for all commuting squares
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Λ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mo ∃
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Lambda[n]_{k} &amp;\to&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;{}^{\exists}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Delta[n] &amp;\to&amp; S
                  }
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \lt n
          %p
            Morphisms with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
            against all left/right fibrations are called
            %strong left/right anodyne
            maps.
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RFib
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  RFib(S) \subset sSet/S
          %p
            for the full
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            on those morphisms that are right fibrations.
          %p
            This is a
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                of right fibrations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+left+fibrations"} model structure for right fibrations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
          %h2#GrothGrpdFibsAreRightKanFibs Motivation: ordinary fibrations in groupoids are right Kan fibrations
          %p
            Ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+fibered+in+groupoids"} categories fibered in groupoids
            have a simple characterization in terms of their
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : Cat \to sSet
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            functor and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : E \to B
            a morphism in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(p) : N(E) \to N(B)
            be the corresponding morphism in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          %p Then
          %p
          #FibrationInGroupoidsAsRightKanFibrations.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon E \to B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+fibered+in+groupoids"} fibration in groupoids
              precisely if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(p) \colon N(E) \to N(B)
              is a right Kan fibration of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %p To see this, first notice the following facts:
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_1 Lemma 1
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeletal"} 2-coskeletal
              = succeed "-spheres" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 3
              have unique fillers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ∀
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mo !
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta[n] &amp;\stackrel{\forall}{\to}&amp; N(C)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\exists !}}
                    \\\
                    \\Delta[n]
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    (n \geq 3)
            %p
              and (implied by that) all
              = succeed "-horns" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 3
              have fillers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Λ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ∀
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ∃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Lambda[n] &amp;\stackrel{\forall}{\to}&amp; N(C)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\exists }}
                    \\\
                    \\Delta[n]
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    (n \gt 3)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma 2
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : E \to B
              is an ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(f) : N(E) \to N(B)
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              with respect to all
              %em inner
              horn inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda[n]_i \hookrightarrow \Delta[n]
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi i
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt i \lt n
          %p
            This is discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+fibration"} inner fibration
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_the_proposition Proof of the proposition
            %p
              From the above lemmas it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(p) : N(E) \to N(B)
              is a right fibration already precisely if it has the right lifting property with respect only to the three horn inclusions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{  \Lambda[n]_n \hookrightarrow \Delta[n] | n = 1,2,3\}
                    \\,.
            %p So we check explicitly what these three conditions amount to
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
                  – The existence of all fillers
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi Λ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mn 1
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo =
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi e
                              %mtd
                                %mi N
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi N
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi p
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                    %mn 0
                                    %mo →
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi f
                              %mtd
                                %mi N
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\Lambda[1]_1 = \Delta^{\{1\}} &amp;\stackrel{e}{\to}&amp; N(E)
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp; {}^{{\hat f}}\nearrow  &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{N(p)}}
                        \\\
                        \\Delta^{\{0 \to 1\}} &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; N(B)
                        }
                %p
                  means that for all objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
                  and morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : b \to p(e)
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
